Rules:
  [C1] Use LINQ for data queries.
  [C2] Use `IAsyncEnumerable` for async streams.
  [C3] Use `Span<T>` for memory efficiency.
  [C4] Use `Memory<T>` for buffer management.
  [C5] Avoid boxing/unboxing.
  [C6] Use `ArrayPool<T>` for buffer pooling.
  [C7] Profile with dotTrace/dotMemory.
  [C8] Use `ValueTask` for high-performance async.

Pros:
  - Rich language features
  - Good performance
  - LINQ expressiveness

Cons:
  - Complex abstractions
  - Memory pressure
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Rust (safer)
  - Go (simpler)
  - C++ (manual control)

State: +

